STUDY 1: LOCKED CAPACITY CHECK DURING sp_register_and_pay (FR-10 / BR-05)
Query: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM REGISTRATION WHERE TicketID = 1001 AND Status = 'Confirmed';
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

[1A] BEFORE (Without Covering Index idx_reg_ticket_status):
-> Aggregate: count(0)  (cost=5084.10 rows=1) (actual time=24.812..24.813 rows=1 loops=1)
    -> Filter: ((registration.TicketID = 1001) and (registration.`Status` = 'Confirmed'))  (cost=5034.05 rows=500) (actual time=0.082..24.710 rows=30 loops=1)
        -> Table scan on REGISTRATION  (cost=5034.05 rows=50004) (actual time=0.061..21.320 rows=50004 loops=1)

[1B] AFTER (With Covering Index idx_reg_ticket_status (TicketID, Status)):
-> Aggregate: count(0)  (cost=9.45 rows=1) (actual time=0.048..0.049 rows=1 loops=1)
    -> Covering index lookup on REGISTRATION using idx_reg_ticket_status (TicketID=1001, Status='Confirmed')  (cost=6.45 rows=30) (actual time=0.021..0.042 rows=30 loops=1)

Empirical Improvement Summary:
  * Access Type:     ALL (Full Table Scan)  --->  ref (Covering Index Only)
  * Rows Examined:   50,004 rows            --->  30 rows (99.94% reduction)
  * Execution Time:  24.813 ms              --->  0.049 ms (506x speedup)

