STUDY 3: PAGINATION SCALABILITY (OFFSET 40000 VS KEYSET SEEK)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

[3A] OFFSET Pagination (LIMIT 50 OFFSET 40000):
-> Limit/Offset: 50/40000 row(s)  (cost=5034.05 rows=50) (actual time=18.420..18.445 rows=50 loops=1)
    -> Index scan on REGISTRATION using PRIMARY  (cost=5034.05 rows=40050) (actual time=0.035..16.890 rows=40050 loops=1)

[3B] Keyset Pagination (WHERE RegistrationID > 41000 ORDER BY RegistrationID ASC LIMIT 50):
-> Limit: 50 row(s)  (cost=15.20 rows=50) (actual time=0.029..0.044 rows=50 loops=1)
    -> Filter: (registration.RegistrationID > 41000)  (cost=15.20 rows=50) (actual time=0.027..0.039 rows=50 loops=1)
        -> Index range scan on REGISTRATION using PRIMARY over (41000 < RegistrationID)  (cost=15.20 rows=50) (actual time=0.026..0.034 rows=50 loops=1)

Empirical Improvement Summary:
  * Rows Scanned:    40,050 rows  --->  50 rows
